  "curationSourceHash": "ecca6fc2619696ea380f519849bebe4526ecb30d6a540db167d609a2efcbaefb",
  "generatedAt": "2026-09-02T11:19:29.738Z",
  "summary": "## PagerDuty Toolkit\n\nArcade toolkit for LLMs to interact with PagerDuty, enabling incident management, on-call scheduling, team inspection, and account activity monitoring via natural language.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- **Incident lifecycle**: Retrieve, list (with filters by status, urgency, service, team, and time), update status (acknowledge, resolve, reopen), and reassign incidents to specific users.\n- **On-call & scheduling**: List on-call entries and schedules to determine who is currently on call and inspect rotation configurations.\n- **Teams, users & services**: List and retrieve teams (including members and linked resources), users (with fuzzy search by name/email), and services (with name search).\n- **Escalation policies**: List and retrieve individual escalation policies by ID.\n- **Activity & audit**: Fetch the account-wide log entry feed showing triggers, acknowledgments, escalations, and resolutions.\n- **Identity**: Resolve the authenticated user's profile, including contact and notification summaries, via `Whoami`.\n\n## OAuth\n\nThis toolkit uses OAuth 2.0 with **PagerDuty** as the identity provider. See the [PagerDuty auth provider docs](https://docs.arcade.dev/en/references/auth-providers/pagerduty) for configuration details."
}